{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446737-m20-books-for-the-future","id":1446737,"title":"M20 Books for the future?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-30T21:45:43-07:00","id":1446737,"title":"M20 Books for the future?","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"> Chatting with some RDs over on Discord and the subject of M20 v M5 came up.<br /> I am happy with M5 and do not feel another edition is needed. But I would like some additional supplements. Such as;<ul><li>A city guide to Mexico City or Rio de Janeiro (more interesting than Las Vegas),</li> <li>A book on the Umbra, all of it if possible,</li> <li>A game similar to Coteries of New York or Night Road,</li> <li>How to give back massages,</li> <li>Information on chantries,</li> </ul><br /> But what do you think? What book or material do you want?<br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T22:04:26-07:00","id":1446741,"title":"","content":"I suspect that might be a new book next year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T05:04:43-07:00","id":1446782,"title":"","content":"If I am picking a city to do for Mage20 I'd go for El Passo/Jurez. That city sits on multiple borders, USA/Mexico, angloamerica/Latin America, developed world/developing world, democracy is under fire in very different ways on both sides of the border. Since all the gods of magic are deities either of the border or the crossroads, a twin city that is both a border and a crossroads is thematically perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T10:10:30-07:00","id":1446807,"title":"","content":"Well after Tome of the Traditions, my top picks would be<br /> <br /> - Tome of the Disparates<br /> - Umbra<br /> - Book of Quiet (that if I had my way reframed the Marauders as being about personal paradigm taken to the extreme of willful reality denial, rather than being about mental illness)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T12:31:03-07:00","id":1446826,"title":"","content":"I would <i>love</i> a city guide. City books are always my favorite sourcebooks to read, because they let us look at concepts in action and give me inspiration for how to design my own cities (assuming I don't just use the city book's). I liked the Book of Chantries a lot for the same reasons. <br /> <br /> Vegas was neat, but I'd like to see a sourcebook on a more mage-centric location. San Francisco would be cool; you have the city's old counterculture and quirky character clashing with the advent of Big Tech and what's probably now a stranglehold of Technocratic dominance. <br /> <br /> Boston would also be cool, but Awakening already covered that in a sourcebook, and its characters are convertible to Ascension with a little tweaking. (Frankly, I liked it more than Vegas, too.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T13:33:38-07:00","id":1446838,"title":"","content":"Book of Crafts.<br /> Book of Alliance.<br /> Book of Orphans.<br /> Umbra book.<br /> <br /> Though I'm pretty sure Brucato is already working on the first three for Storytellers Vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T23:39:52-07:00","id":1446921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446737-m20-books-for-the-future?p=1446838#post1446838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of Crafts.<br /> Book of Alliance.<br /> Book of Orphans.<br /> Umbra book.<br /> <br /> Though I'm pretty sure Brucato is already working on the first three for Storytellers Vault.</div> </div> </div> </div>so the Crafts book would be on those Crafts who aren\u2019t in the Disparate alliance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:09:53-07:00","id":1446940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446737-m20-books-for-the-future?p=1446921#post1446921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so the Crafts book would be on those Crafts who aren\u2019t in the Disparate alliance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope so. Many of them would be fun to know about. Like the Fringe Walkers that were mentioned once in the first edition main book and ignored ever after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T05:07:41-07:00","id":1446955,"title":"","content":"First of all I would love to get the M20 that are already teased in the core book to get translated to german too.<br /> Then I would agree an orphan book would make much sense because M20 has the orphans predestinated for being Orphan as a starter.<br /> Then I do not know if they already have it but a detailed book about familiars I would love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T11:05:56-07:00","id":1447002,"title":"","content":"A Tome of the Disparates and/or Unaligned Crafts would be great. A new book on the Umbra would be even greater, a Guide to the Otherworlds. Mage is the only game line that can literally go anywhere, but there is just too much to be included in just one chapter of one book. The Book of Worlds was my first Mage supplement, but it was only after I started getting into the other WOD games that I realized how much was missing. I mean, it came out just after Wraith 2nd and Changeling 1st, so details on the Underworld and the Dreaming were slightly off and incomplete. When Infinite Tapestry came out, so much material from Mage 1st and 2nd were lost, and details for the rest of the Umbra were relegated to &quot;check the game line&quot; for more information. There wasn't even information on the newest additions, such as the 1,000 Hells and Demon pocket dimensions. Don't get me wrong, it did provide some great information for the Revised setting, I just loved the first book so much. A new book updating every Umbra location from a Mage POV, particularly the Mage-centric ones, could bridge the differences between the two. I've been thinking about something along these lines for months, along with a totally new take on the WOD cosmology. A companion book focusing on a Mage version of Axis Mundi: the Book of Spirits would allow for more info in the main book. Maybe a second add on for a more detailed look on Bygones, familiars, and other Umbral beings in the material world. This is a dream project of mine, if you couldn't tell. I've also been thinking about related works for how other splats handle the Otherworlds, including Werewolves outside of the Middle Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T15:51:31-07:00","id":1447053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446737-m20-books-for-the-future?p=1446921#post1446921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so the Crafts book would be on those Crafts who aren\u2019t in the Disparate alliance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather not have the official publication line make that distinction. What I'd like to see in a M20 Book of Crafts/Tome of the Disparates would be for the bulk of the book to be write-ups of individual Crafts on their own terms, save for each write-up having a section detailing what that Craft's relations with the Alliance might be like, which could range from \u201cthey've signed up\u201d to \u201cthey're on friendly terms, but are keeping their distance for now\u201d to \u201cthey actively distrust the Alliance, and want nothing to do with it\u201d to \u201cthey actively oppose the Alliance\u201d to \u201cwhat Alliance?\u201d. <br /> <br /> Then have a section on the Alliance itself, focused mainly on the various challenges it faces (\u201chow it might fail\u201d) and ways to deal with them (\u201chow it might succeed\u201d). This section would <i>almost</i> be like yet another Craft write-up in terms of its significance to the book: use it, or don't; your choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T16:03:55-07:00","id":1447054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1446737-m20-books-for-the-future?p=1447002#post1447002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Tome of the Disparates and/or Unaligned Crafts would be great. A new book on the Umbra would be even greater, a Guide to the Otherworlds. Mage is the only game line that can literally go anywhere, but there is just too much to be included in just one chapter of one book. The Book of Worlds was my first Mage supplement, but it was only after I started getting into the other WOD games that I realized how much was missing. I mean, it came out just after Wraith 2nd and Changeling 1st, so details on the Underworld and the Dreaming were slightly off and incomplete. When Infinite Tapestry came out, so much material from Mage 1st and 2nd were lost, and details for the rest of the Umbra were relegated to &amp;quot;check the game line&amp;quot; for more information. There wasn't even information on the newest additions, such as the 1,000 Hells and Demon pocket dimensions. Don't get me wrong, it did provide some great information for the Revised setting, I just loved the first book so much. A new book updating every Umbra location from a Mage POV, particularly the Mage-centric ones, could bridge the differences between the two. I've been thinking about something along these lines for months, along with a totally new take on the WOD cosmology. A companion book focusing on a Mage version of Axis Mundi: the Book of Spirits would allow for more info in the main book. Maybe a second add on for a more detailed look on Bygones, familiars, and other Umbral beings in the material world. This is a dream project of mine, if you couldn't tell. I've also been thinking about related works for how other splats handle the Otherworlds, including Werewolves outside of the Middle Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want that as a Mage supplement; I want that as a general World of Darkness supplement. That said, it would likely fit the \u201cX20\u201d pattern of having a massive page count, due to the effort to fit so many diverse elements into one book. <br /> <br /> Conversely, I'm not sure that I'd want, say, the Maya to actually <i>be</i> the Dreaming of Changeling fame. Let it be to the Dreaming as the Pattern Web is to the Digital Web; or something to that effect. <br /> <br /> But then, I'm a fan of the Chronicles of Darkness notion that \u201cotherworlds\u201d is just a catch-all phrase for \u201canything that isn't the physical world\u201d, and that there isn't some grand unified organizing principle behind it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T11:25:17-07:00","id":1447422,"title":"","content":"In a ridiculous never going to happen series of books I'd want if we were still on the supplement treadmill<br /> <br /> - Book on the High Umbra, and Umbrood Courts, + the Shard and Shade Realms of Mind<br /> - WtA crossover book, examining Mages in Middle Umbra and interaction with Triat struggles, + Shard and Shade Realms of Spirit<br /> - WtO crossover book, examining Mages in the Low Umbra, + Shard and Shade Realms of Entropy<br /> - Digital Web 3.0, Mount Qaf, and the Shard and Shade Realms of Correspondence<br /> - Hollow Earth, and the Shard and Shade Realms of Matter<br /> - Book on time travel options, historic settings, divergent timelines, and the Mirror Zone/Everett Volumes, + Shard and Shade Realms of Time<br /> - Book on the Horizon (as in many Realms, not just &quot;Horizon&quot; the old Trad capital), and deep space including penumbral planets, + Shard and Shade Realms of Forces<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I don't have great ideas for what to tie to the Realms of Life and Prime, or where to do the Changeling Crossover (honestly C20 getting its own book on the Dreaming is a way higher priority than Mage getting a Maya/Crossover Guide)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:58:27-07:00","id":1447472,"title":"","content":"If we are into dreams and desires, I want a Space Opera book.<br /> <br /> Following the model of Tales of Magick Dark Adventure, I suggest Genre books. Each book in the series would be about 150 pages long and would cover four or five genres per book. Example, you might do Gothic Romance, Steampunk, Westerns, and Pirate stories in one book. Space Opera, Cyberpunk, Planetary Romance, and Superheroes in another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}